&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote - North America (Open to candidates across the Americas aligned time zones, with a preference for Eastern Time Zone)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fueled is a leading digital strategy, design, and engineering agency. We are a 300+ person team that has designed and built hundreds of digital products and experiences for brands like Google, Apple, The New York Times, ESPN, Victoria’s Secret, MGM Resorts, Albertsons, and CLEAR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;VP of Client Growth&lt;/strong&gt; at Fueled, you’ll own the long-term health, retention, and growth of our client portfolio. This senior leadership role is for someone who sees client relationships as both an art and a business driver. You’ll lead the Client Growth organization, define how we partner with clients post-sale, and turn trust into measurable growth through renewals, scope expansion, and multi-year partnerships. As a member of the GTM Leadership Team, you’ll oversee key client relationships while building the team, playbook, and commercial discipline needed to turn strong client outcomes into a durable revenue engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Intentionally remote and globally distributed across six continents, our team thrives in a culture that values flexibility, creativity, and cutting-edge technology. Together, we’re shaping the future of digital experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strategic account practices and engagement standards that strengthen portfolio performance and client continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale the commercial discipline, operating rhythms, and service models that drive sustainable Net Revenue Retention (NRR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop senior client growth leaders capable of influencing executive stakeholders and leading complex enterprise relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with GTM, Delivery, and Practice Leadership to ensure account plans are profitable, scalable, and aligned to client outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance portfolio visibility and decision-making through clear forecasting, health metrics, renewal planning, and expansion pipeline management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will achieve:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow and protect recurring revenue through stronger retention, account expansion, and long-term client investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a high-performing Client Growth function with clear accountability, strong talent development, and measurable commercial impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to greater client confidence and strategic alignment through proactive business reviews and executive engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance operational efficiency and profitability by improving forecasting accuracy, pricing alignment, staffing plans, and margin management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the evolution of the agency’s client growth strategy by identifying emerging opportunities, reducing churn risk, and strengthening collaboration between New Business and Delivery teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a builder by nature, with a track record of scaling client growth or account management organizations in agency, consulting, or professional services environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong commercial mindset and know how to turn trusted client relationships into sustainable business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are well-versed in commercial strategy, including pricing, scoping, contract negotiation, margin management, and portfolio forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re confident partnering with senior client stakeholders and executive teams, with the judgment to influence, challenge, and build trust at the highest levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited by building operational rigor and cross-functional alignment, knowing that sustainable growth comes from exceptional delivery, strong teams, and disciplined execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
